{"name":"Wallflower White","hex":"#e4e3e6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wallflower","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several short-lived herbs or shrubs of the Erysimum genus with bright yellow to red flowers.","Gastrolobium grandiflorum, a poisonous bushy shrub, endemic to Australia."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stand shyly apart from a dance, waiting to be asked to join in."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wallflower"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Erysimum","blocks":[{"text":"Erysimum, or wallflower, is a genus of flowering plants in the cabbage family, Brassicaceae. It includes more than 150 species, both popular garden plants and many wild forms. Erysimum is characterised by star-shaped trichomes growing from the stem, with yellow, red, pink or orange flowers and multiseeded seed pods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/1c/Erysimum-scoparium.jpg/330px-Erysimum-scoparium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erysimum"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/120px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/250px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg/120px-Erysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErysimum_wittmanii_a1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/120px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/250px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg/120px-ErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErysimumChelseaJacket.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Erysimum_helveticum.jpg/120px-Erysimum_helveticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Erysimum_helveticum.jpg/250px-Erysimum_helveticum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna